==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=respiration}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|respiracioun}}, borrowed from {{bor|en|la|respiratio|respiratio, respirationis}}, from {{m|la|respirare}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɹɛspɪˈɹeɪʃən/|lang=en}}
* {{hyph|res|pi|ra|tion|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|eɪʃən|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|respiration (physiology)}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# The process of [[inhaling]] and [[exhaling]]; [[breathing]], [[breath]].
# An act of [[breathing]]; a [[breath]].
#* '''1931''', William Faulkner, ''Sanctuary'', Vintage 1993, p. 76:
#*: Gowan snored, each '''respiration''' choking to a huddle fall, as though he would never breathe again.
# Any similar process in an organism that lacks [[lungs]] that exchanges [[gas]]es with its [[environment]].
# The process by which [[cell]]s obtain [[chemical]] [[energy]] by the consumption of [[oxygen]] and the release of [[carbon dioxide]].

